0..78 Comment "// A method that answers a place. A method whose receiver\'s mode is a variable"
79..157 Comment "// of its implicit block, `self : m T` under `@[m : Mode]`, answers a place of"
158..227 Comment "// its receiver at that mode, `-F View[m](a)`: its body is the place,"
228..294 Comment "// `self[i]`, and a call is the access to it. A call with a block,"
295..373 Comment "// `xs.first() as w { … }`, lends the place at the mode the block asks — a"
374..453 Comment "// resume or an abort through `w` asks an exclusive lend, a read alone a shared"
454..532 Comment "// one — and a call without one reads the place. One body serves every mode,"
533..610 Comment "// as an explicit object parameter deduces its receiver\'s qualifiers (Ažman,"
611..684 Comment "// Brand, Deane and Revzin, \"Deducing this\", C++ proposal P0847R7, 2021)."
686..720 Comment "// The list each call below holds."
